      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "Colorectal laterally spreading tumors (LSTs) larger than 20 mm are significant precursors to colorectal cancer. Endoscopic submucosal dissection (ESD) and endoscopic mucosal resection (EMR) are widely used treatments, but their comparative efficacy and safety remain controversial.",
      "reason": "The abstract background describes the current state of knowledge (LSTs as cancer precursors; ESD and EMR widely used) and an uncertainty (comparative efficacy and safety remain controversial). However, the Introduction section itself was not retrieved, so the full rationale description cannot be verified beyond the abstract."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PARTIAL",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "This systematic review and meta-analysis aimed to compare ESD and EMR in terms of local recurrence, perforation, and delayed bleeding for colorectal LSTs > 20 mm.",
      "reason": "The aim of the review is stated and the controversy noted in the background implies a need, but the importance and need for conducting the review are not explicitly argued (no retrieved Introduction text explaining why the review is needed)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No retrieved evidence cites or discusses previous systematic reviews on ESD versus EMR for colorectal LSTs > 20 mm, nor explains the need for an update or replication relative to prior reviews."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No retrieved evidence describes a proposed mechanism of action for ESD or EMR (e.g., how en bloc versus piecemeal resection affects recurrence risk)."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "MISSING",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "No retrieved evidence presents or discusses a logic model relating intervention components to outcomes; the retrieved sections (methods, results, limitations) contain no such material."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 70
}

